Arithmetic Operators in C Programming

Today, I learned about arithmetic operators in C programming. 
Arithmetic operators are used to perform mathematical calculations on variables and values.

Types of Arithmetic Operators

Operator  |	Name	        |         Description
----------|-----------------|---------------------------------------
+	      |   Addition	    |         Adds two values
-	      | Subtraction	    | Subtracts one value from another
*	      | Multiplication  |      Multiplies two values
/	      |   Division	    |   Divides one value by another
%	      |   Modulus       | Returns the remainder after division
++        |  Increment      | 
--        |  Decrement      |
--------------------------------------------------------------------


Important Points I Learned

Arithmetic operators are used to perform mathematical operations.
The + operator adds two numbers.
The - operator subtracts numbers.
The * operator multiplies numbers.
The / operator performs division. When both operands are integers, the fractional part is discarded.
The % operator returns the remainder and works with integer operands.
The -- operator decrements numbers by 1.
The ++ operator increments numbers by 1.
Division and modulus by zero must be avoided.

Conclusion

Today, I learned how to use arithmetic operators in C programming .
